DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/eve
 nts/2026/09/28/montgomery-fellow-lunch-with-water-scientist/\nhttps://appl
 y.gs.dartmouth.edu/register/?id=bd914235-6f3a-48a7-a9fb-88105c846e1b\nhttp
 s://montgomery.dartmouth.edu/people/ryan-e-emanuel\nhttps://guarinigrad.da
 rtmouth.edu\n\nDescription:\nJoin Water Scientist Ryan E. Emanuel for a Mo
 ntgomery Fellow lunch discussion\nRyan E. Emanuel is a hydrologist and com
 munity-engaged scholar at Duke University’s Nicholas School of the Envir
 onment\, where he is an associate professor of hydrology and co-chair of D
 uke’s program in Community Engagement and Environmental Justice.\nHis re
 search interests span the environmental sciences and extend into history\,
  Indigenous studies\, environmental justice\, and research ethics. Emanuel
  and his research group have partnered with Tribal Nations\, environmental
  organizations\, and community groups to conduct research and science-base
 d advocacy\, and their work has influenced public policies and corporate a
 ctions related to environmental justice and tribal engagement.\nFor more g
 o to\nhttps://montgomery.dartmouth.edu/people/ryan-e-emanuel\n\nSponsor / 
 organizer: GuariniGRAD\n\nAudience: Graduate students\, postdocs\n\nSource
 : Guarini\n\nWhy this was included: food or meal keyword in title\n\nFood 
 availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details before a
 ttending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T145501Z
LOCATION:Anonymous Hall\, 113 Guarini Conference Room
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://guarinigrad.dartmouth.edu/events/2026/09/28/montgomery-fellow-
 lunch-with-water-scientist/
