DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82773\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdUrwMOEvbbvop2aj
 ySHtNWBbFpHe_yjsbplcN-8sR2_yuFRA/viewform?usp=header\n\nDescription:\nJoin
  the Climate Collaborative and Montgomery Fellows Program for a homemade p
 izza dinner at the Dartmouth Organic Farm with Fellow Ryan Emanuel. Pizza 
 fixings and good times provided! Please\nRSVP here\n!\nRyan E. Emanuel is 
 a hydrologist and community-engaged scholar at Duke University’s Nichola
 s School of the Environment\, where he is an associate professor of hydrol
 ogy and co-chair of Duke’s program in Community Engagement and Environme
 ntal Justice.\nHis research interests span the environmental sciences and 
 extend into history\, Indigenous studies\, environmental justice\, and res
 earch ethics. Emanuel and his research group have partnered with Tribal Na
 tions\, environmental organizations\, and community groups to conduct rese
 arch and science-based advocacy\, and their work has influenced public pol
 icies and corporate actions related to environmental justice and tribal en
 gagement.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Climate Collaborative\, Montgomery Fello
 ws Program\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was includ
 ed: food or meal keyword in title\n\nFood availability is inferred from th
 e source listing\; verify details before attending.
