BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:University Seminar: Debt and Credit
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T121500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T134500
DTSTAMP:20260925T145501Z
UID:dartmouth-82864@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82864\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScNjqTASzpqvVofOM
 AB46-ZkIfyqc55GyPD3H9VIe-RuoqpFw/viewform\n\nDescription:\nUniversity Semi
 nar on Debt and Credit\nwill convene twice per term over the coming year.\
 nThe seminar takes up debt and credit as frameworks that shape economic an
 d institutional life\, moral reasoning\, and social relations. Debt and cr
 edit function as financial instruments\, of course\, but they also work as
  metaphors and organizing principles across religion\, law\, education\, m
 edicine\, and environmental policy. Our aim is not to arrive at a unified 
 thesis but to build an ongoing forum where colleagues can share work in pr
 ogress\, test ideas\, and see how a shared conceptual vocabulary connects 
 otherwise distant fields. We are hoping for a genuinely interdisciplinary 
 group\, and no disciplinary vantage point is off the table.\nOur first mee
 ting will have a\ncatered lunch by Salubre.\nThe initial seminar will cen
 ter on a reading to discuss together:\nDavid Graeber\, chapter 1\, "On th
 e Experience of Moral Confusion\," from\nDebt: The First 5000 Years\n(20 p
 p.)\; which you will receive upon registration.\nPlease click\nhere\nto co
 nfirm your interest and let us know about any dietary restrictions. If you
  are not able to make the first meeting but would like to remain on the ma
 iling list for information about future meetings\, please also use the for
 m to confirm interest.\n\nSponsor / organizer: French and Italian Departme
 nt\, Leslie Center for the Humanities\, Religion Department\n\nAudience: A
 lumni\, Faculty\, Postdoc\, Staff\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was inc
 luded: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service context\n
 \nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details b
 efore attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T145501Z
LOCATION:Haldeman 246
